# Run acceptance evidence — orchid self-hosting hardening run

Integration head at acceptance: `a6bc7f8420c0ebe0b836ec27aa856253f38ab6ae`
Shipped version at acceptance: `1.0.0-beta.1`

## How this was checked

`bash scripts/ci-local.sh --bash /bin/bash`, run against the MERGED
integration checkout — not against any individual task candidate. `orchid
verify` is task-scoped; the criteria below are run-scoped, so they are proven
on the tree as it will be merged to main. Result: **CI PASS**, 0 failures
across 433 lines of output.

## Run-level acceptance criteria, one by one

- **`bash tests/run.sh` passes** — PASS. Included in the ci-local gate above.
- **All new focused tests pass independently** — PASS. `tests/run.sh`
  auto-discovers by glob, so every suite added by this run (test_drive*,
  test_task_arbitrate, test_run_boundary, test_orchestrator_command,
  test_start*, test_beta_qualification, test_e2e_release_rehearsal,
  INV-13, INV-14) is executed by the same pass.
- **`bash -n` passes for every shipped shell script under Bash 3.2** — PASS.
  ci-local's first stage: 145 shipped scripts, `/bin/bash`.
- **The configured ShellCheck gate passes** — PASS, at zero warnings. This
  criterion was FAILING for most of the run behind a gate nothing invoked
  (see L016); T007 cleared 17 inherited findings and it has been green since.
- **Documentation and CLI help agree with implemented behavior** — PASS.
  ci-local's Documentation checks stage.
- **A local end-to-end rehearsal demonstrates the unattended trust refusal,
  acknowledged deterministic drive, one-command setup, and beta qualification
  path without any network or external mutation** — PASS, via
  `tests/test_e2e_release_rehearsal.sh`, which walks all seven phases with
  every network tool, vendor CLI, notify sender and remote-capable git
  subcommand shimmed to log-and-fail, and asserts the tripwire log is empty
  at the end. Its self-test now stands on a disposable repository inside the
  private root with no remote, so a total shim failure reaches a scratch
  directory rather than a real origin.

## What this evidence does NOT claim

Stated explicitly because the requirements forbid implying otherwise:

- **No third-party beta run has occurred.** The harness and checklist exist
  and are exercised against local fixtures only. Genuine external
  qualification remains operator-owned follow-up work.
- **Nothing was published, pushed, tagged, deployed, or sent to a remote** at
  any point in this run.
- **Reviewer independence was DEGRADED for most tasks.** codex and
  codex-review were credit-exhausted throughout; agy is an inline diff-only
  reviewer whose adapter refuses a diff over `agy_max_bytes`, so it was
  structurally excluded from every task whose diff exceeded ~100KB. T001,
  T002, T003, T005 and T006 landed with session-independent review only
  (claude reviewing claude). T007 and T008 had genuine engine-independent
  review. This is recorded, not papered over.
- **Known defects ship.** Accepted deliberately, each with an arbitration
  entry: T002's HIGH (`drive_implementing` lacks the liveness guard its
  sibling arms carry, so a failed implementer can spawn duplicate concurrent
  implementers into one worktree) plus seven further findings; T003's four
  mediums including an `.orchid/tasks/` idempotence break against an explicit
  acceptance criterion; and T005's six ledger items, notably that the
  rehearsal now runs inside `release.sh`'s extracted archive where its
  source-checkout snapshots pass vacuously.

## What this run found in orchid itself

18 lessons recorded (L001–L018). The five that would matter most to anyone
picking this up:

- **L013** — shell injection in shipped 1.0.0: `verb_lock_acquire` eval'd a
  jq-authored shell fragment built from a lock's `owner.json` with `.pid`
  unquoted. Reproduced with a working payload; fixed at both call sites with
  a test that fails on the vulnerable form.
- **L009** — headless deadlock: `orchid merge`'s rebase invalidates the
  formula pin, and no in-loop actor can re-pin it.
- **L018** — orchid executes whatever is in the working tree, so a stale
  integration checkout silently runs pre-merge code. It cost this run a full
  day of its own merged improvements before it was noticed.
- **L016** — the release gate T004 built was never invoked by any task
  dispatched after it. "It exists in the repo" and "it runs" are different
  facts.
- **L005** — `assert_match` piped into `grep -q` under `pipefail` across 892
  call sites, in the shared helper every test in the suite stands on.

None of these were findable by reading. Each surfaced because the system was
driven hard against itself.
